>> title: Fudgy Cocoa Brownies
>> category: Bars & Brownies
>> tags: chocolate, cocoa, walnuts, dessert, oven
>> counters: Bakery, Diner
>> aka: brownie, fudge brownies, cocoa brownies, brownie a la mode
>> pairs-with: french-vanilla-ice-cream
>> servings: 9
>> time: 45 min

Line an #8x8-in pan{} with parchment, leaving an overhang on two sides.

Preheat the #oven{} to 325°F (165°C).

Melt @unsalted butter{10%Tbs}(140 g), @granulated sugar{1 1/4%cup}(250 g), @unsweetened cocoa powder{3/4%cup}(65 g), @table salt{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g) together in a #double boiler{}.

Stir @&(~1)cocoa mixture{} with @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL).

>> step: beat in one at a time, 40 strokes each
Beat @&(~1)mixture{} with @eggs{2%large}(100 g), one at a time and 40 strokes each.

Stir in @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup}(65 g), @chopped toasted walnuts{2/3%cup}(60 g) to @&(~1)batter{}.

Bake @&(~1)batter{} at 325°F for ~{25%min}.
